  "id": "haitian_konbit_work_songs",
  "name": "Konbit songs (Haitian collective work songs)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Songs of the konbit (coumbite), the collective work party in which Haitian farmers clear or hoe a neighbour's field together. A song leader (simidor) improvises lines, often teasing or topical, that the work gang answers while a drummer keeps the hoes moving in time; Harold Courlander described and recorded the practice, and Alan Lomax recorded work songs in Haiti in 1936-37.",
  "recipe": "classic mid-1930s konbit songs, field Work. single leader group response. acoustic membrane drum, field hoe work hoe. field recording. small-diaphragm pencil condenser, portable field-recorder pre. tape 15ips.",
